# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS tracked. The stock Rust template ignores it on the old
# libraries-do-not-commit-it rule, but this workspace publishes a binary
# (glossia-cli), Cargo now recommends committing it for every project, and
# it ships inside the published .crate either way -- so leaving it untracked
# only meant shipping a resolution nobody had tested. It matters more here
# than most: verification-by-re-render makes generator behaviour part of the
# format, so a semver-compatible dependency bump can move every rendering,
# which is the same hazard the explicit ChaCha12 pin guards on its own axis.

